{
  "A window or dialog built on the native `<dialog>` element. A single form can be shown as modeless or modal, depending on how you open it. It has a title bar, can be moved, resized, minimized and maximized, and Enter and Escape activate its buttons. Forms can open other forms, and `messageBox` and `confirm` cover common prompts.": "",
  "In JSX, `x-model` shows the form while the value is true and writes `false` when the user closes it. The form is hidden rather than disposed, and it lives with its parent. Programmatically, a form, usually a class with a `view()` method, opens with `show(host)` or `showDialog(host)`. It is added to the host and disposed when it closes.": "",
  "Modal and modeless": "Modal ve modeless",
  "`show()` keeps the page usable. Several modeless windows can stack, and clicking one brings it to the front. `showDialog()` blocks everything else until it closes, and a modal form opened from another modal form blocks that form too.": "",
  "Title bar and frame": "Başlık çubuğu ve çerçeve",
  "The title bar shows the icon, the title and the buttons you enable. The form moves by its title bar and stays inside the viewport. It resizes from its edges and corners, down to the `window.min-*` tokens. Each of these features has its own setting.": "",
  "Default and cancel buttons": "Varsayılan ve iptal düğmeleri",
  "Enter in a single-line field clicks `acceptButton`, and Escape clicks `cancelButton`. Without a cancel button, `closeOnEscape` decides. It is on for modal forms and off for modeless ones.": "",
  "`onClosing` can keep the form open, in this case while it has unsaved changes. `reason` distinguishes a user action (close button, Escape) from a programmatic close and from the owner being disposed.": "",
  "Message boxes": "İleti kutuları",
  "`messageBox` shows a modal message with buttons and resolves with the result of the button pressed. `confirm` asks OK or Cancel and resolves to `true` or `false`. Caution and danger boxes are alert dialogs, and a danger box starts on its safe button.": "",
  "Inside a modal form, Tab cycles within it. From a modeless form, it continues to the page.": "",
  "Clicks `cancelButton`. Otherwise, it closes the form when `closeOnEscape` is on, which is the default for modal forms.": "",
  "In a single-line field, clicks `acceptButton`. This does not apply in a text area or on a button.": "",
  "Access keys work inside the front window. While a modal form is open, they work only inside it.": "",
  "Moved and resized with the pointer. There are no built-in keys, but an application can add them with `form.addShortcut(...)` and the `left`, `top`, `width` and `height` properties.": "",
  "A native `<dialog>`, using `showModal()` for a modal form, which makes the page inert, and `show()` for a modeless one.": "",
  "`role=\"dialog\"` (`alertdialog` with `alert`), `aria-modal=\"true\"` when modal, and named by its title through `aria-labelledby`.": "",
  "A message box is described by its text (`aria-describedby`).": "İleti kutusu metniyle açıklanır (`aria-describedby`).",
  "On open, focus goes to `[autofocus]`, the first field, the accept button or the first control. On close, it returns to where it was. It never falls to `<body>`.": "",
  "Named from `uiLocale` (Minimize, Maximize, Restore, Close).": "Adını `uiLocale` dosyasından alır (Küçült, Büyüt, Geri yükle, Kapat).",
  "A short fade using the motion tokens, removed when the user prefers reduced motion.": "",
  "The title bar buttons and the `ok`, `cancel`, `yes` and `no` buttons of a message box get their names from `uiLocale.strings`.": "",
  "The `<dialog>`. `data-state` (`normal`, `minimized`, `maximized`), `data-modal`, `data-active`, `data-placed`, `data-docked`, `data-resizable`, `data-movable`, `data-dragging`.": "`<dialog>`. `data-state` (`normal`, `minimized`, `maximized`), `data-modal`, `data-active`, `data-placed`, `data-docked`, `data-resizable`, `data-movable`, `data-dragging`.",
  "The title bar and its parts.": "Başlık çubuğu ve parçaları.",
  "The content area and the button row.": "",
  "The resize handles.": "Boyutlandırma tutamaçları.",
  "The chip a minimized form leaves in its `minimizeTarget`.": "Küçültülen formun `minimizeTarget` içinde bıraktığı chip.",
  "The content of a message box, with `data-tone`.": "",
  "The size and position the form sets on itself.": "",
  "Units: the backdrop of a modal form, and the surface (`active`, `dialog` for a modal form, `maximized`).": "",
  "Units: the title bar (`active`, `dialog`), its icon, the title (`dialog`) and its buttons.": "Unit'ler: başlık çubuğu (`active`, `dialog`), icon'u, başlık (`dialog`) ve düğmeleri.",
  "Units: the content area, the button row and the resize grips (`corner`).": "",
  "The title bar height (from the design system `bar.*` tokens), and the position of the title and its buttons.": "",
  "The minimum size and the margin kept around the form.": "",
  "The resize handles, and the distance it animates in from.": "",
  "Message boxes: units for the content and its tone glyph (per tone), and their width.": "İleti kutuları: içerik ve ton glyph'i için unit'ler (tona göre) ve genişlikleri.",
  "Opened through `value`, the form is modal.": "",
  "The title in the title bar, which also names the form. This is the same property as `text`.": "",
  "Content for the content area, in addition to JSX children and `view()`.": "",
  "A non-scrolling row below the content, for buttons.": "",
  "An icon at the start of the title bar.": "Başlık çubuğunun başında icon.",
  "Shows the close button.": "",
  "Shows the minimize button, on modeless forms only.": "",
  "Shows the maximize button. Double-clicking the title bar does the same.": "",
  "Allows resizing from the edges and corners.": "",
  "Allows moving by dragging the title bar, within the viewport.": "",
  "`true` for modal forms, `false` for modeless forms": "",
  "Closes the form with `cancel` on Escape when there is no `cancelButton`.": "",
  "The button Enter clicks from a single-line field.": "",
  "The button Escape clicks.": "Escape'in tıkladığı düğme.",
  "Where a minimized form leaves a chip that restores it. Without it, the form collapses to its title bar.": "",
  "`center`, or `manual` at `left` and `top`.": "`center` ya da `left` ve `top` konumunda `manual`.",
  "With `manual`, the position from the start edge (the right edge in RTL) and the top. A number is in pixels.": "",
  "Content size": "",
  "A CSS length. A number is in pixels.": "",
  "`role=\"alertdialog\"`, for urgent content.": "",
  "By default, a form added to the host by `show` or `showDialog` is disposed, and a JSX form is hidden.": "",
  "Accepts a value or a function, the same as the prop. `left`, `top`, `width` and `height` track moving and resizing by the user.": "",
  "How the form closed, or will close. `close()` without an argument uses this value. It is `cancel` on open.": "",
  "Indicate whether the form is open, whether it is modal, and whether it is the front window of the page.": "",
  "The child control that has focus, or last had it.": "",
  "The content area element.": "İçerik alanı öğesi.",
  "Shows the form as modeless in `host` (a component or the application). It is disposed with `disposeRef`, or with the host.": "",
  "Shows the form as modal and resolves with the result when it closes.": "",
  "Brings it to the front with focus on its last active control.": "Son etkin control'üne odaklanarak öne getirir.",
  "These set `windowState`.": "",
  "Centers it in the viewport.": "",
  "Returns focus to its last active control.": "",
  "Runs before the first show, and is where to populate the form.": "",
  "Occur when it becomes the front window and when another window takes over.": "",
  "Occurs before it closes. `e`: `{ result, reason, source, cancel }`. Set `cancel = true` to keep it open, unless its owner is being disposed.": "",
  "Occurs after it closes. `e`: `{ result, reason, source }`, where `reason` is `user` (close button, Escape), `code` or `owner`.": "",
  "Helper functions": "",
  "Shows a modal message: `title`, `text`, `buttons` (`ok`, `cancel`, `yes`, `no` or `{ text, result, tone }`), `tone` (`info`, `success`, `caution`, `danger`), `defaultButton` and `host`.": "",
  "Shows OK and Cancel, and resolves to `true` for OK.": ""
}
